WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.500
Series. Muriel. The Little Alchemist. Season 1, Episode 1.

00:09.200 --> 00:12.000
Hi there. I'm Morel and I'm a Little Alchemist.

00:12.100 --> 00:15.100
That means I love mixing things together to make magic.

00:15.200 --> 00:16.900
I mean, chemistry happen.

00:21.700 --> 00:26.500
Some people think chemistry is boring, but they just don't know how exciting it can be.

00:26.900 --> 00:29.800
Watch this. When I mix these two liquids,

00:30.400 --> 00:33.600
boom, a colorful explosion of foam.

00:33.800 --> 00:36.200
That's the reaction between an acid and a base.

00:36.400 --> 00:38.400
It's like they're having a bubbly party.

00:43.800 --> 00:47.700
And sometimes if I'm really careful, I can make something truly magical.

00:53.600 --> 00:57.400
And in my village, most kids like to play outside,

00:57.600 --> 01:00.700
but I love staying in my lab creating colorful potions.

01:02.100 --> 01:05.300
Morel, why don't you come play with us instead of doing weird experiments?

01:05.800 --> 01:07.600
But this is how I play.

01:07.900 --> 01:10.100
Every experiment is like a new adventure.

01:10.600 --> 01:14.900
One day, I'll show everyone how amazing and useful chemistry can be.

01:18.700 --> 01:20.700
Oh no, our crops are failing. What will we do?

01:21.000 --> 01:23.000
We'll all go hungry if we can't grow food.

01:23.300 --> 01:26.500
Maybe I can help. I'll mix up something special in my lab.

01:28.400 --> 01:30.400
First, we need to understand the problem.

01:30.700 --> 01:32.900
The soil must be missing something important.

01:33.200 --> 01:37.900
Let's see. A pinch of this, a dash of that, and a whole lot of determination.

01:42.400 --> 01:45.400
This blue powder is a special fertilizer.

01:45.700 --> 01:47.900
It's full of nutrients that plants love.

01:48.400 --> 01:50.900
This time, I'll add a little bit of sparkle dust.

01:51.200 --> 01:52.900
I mean, catalyst.

01:53.700 --> 01:56.400
A catalyst is something that helps a chemical reaction

01:56.400 --> 01:59.900
happen faster, like magic, but scientific.

02:03.400 --> 02:04.900
It's working.

02:05.400 --> 02:07.900
The potion is glowing and bubbling just right.

02:08.400 --> 02:09.900
The color tells me it's perfect.

02:10.400 --> 02:13.900
In chemistry, color changes often mean something important is happening.

02:17.400 --> 02:19.900
Here, Mr. Farmer, try pouring this on your crops.

02:20.400 --> 02:21.900
Are you sure about this, Morel?

02:22.400 --> 02:23.900
Trust in chemistry, Mr. Farmer.

02:24.400 --> 02:25.900
It's never let me down before.

02:27.400 --> 02:31.900
Now we wait. Chemical reactions can take time, just like growing plants.

02:35.400 --> 02:36.900
Look, the plants are starting to perk up.

02:37.400 --> 02:38.900
I can't believe my eyes.

02:39.400 --> 02:41.900
Wow, the plants are growing bigger and healthier than ever.

02:46.400 --> 02:47.900
Morel, you're a hero. How did you do it?

02:48.400 --> 02:50.900
It's all thanks to the magic of chemistry.

02:51.400 --> 02:53.900
The potion I made had just the right balance of nutrients

02:53.900 --> 02:55.400
It's like cooking, but for plants.

02:55.900 --> 02:58.400
That's so cool. Can you teach us how to do that?

02:58.900 --> 03:01.400
Of course. Who wants to learn how to make potions?

03:01.900 --> 03:03.400
We do. We do.

03:05.900 --> 03:08.400
Great. Let's start with something simple and fun.

03:08.900 --> 03:10.400
We'll make a color-changing potion.

03:10.900 --> 03:12.400
Remember, safety first.

03:15.900 --> 03:17.400
Wow, my potion turned from clear to purple.

03:17.900 --> 03:21.400
That's right. The indicator we added changes the color of the potion.

03:21.400 --> 03:26.900
That's right. The indicator we added changes color based on whether the solution is acidic or basic.

03:30.400 --> 03:32.900
So are you ready to become a little alchemist, too?

03:33.400 --> 03:35.900
Remember, with chemistry, anything is possible.

